From e0ab696456125b051600d0b09f6fc9916e6752c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:51:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommax: ipq50xx: ax3000t-v2: allow an in-place sysupgrade

platform_check_image refused every sysupgrade on the AX3000T v2 that did
not run from the RAM-booted initramfs: the stock U-Boot was taken to
attach only a kernel UBI that was freshly ubiformatted, so an in-place
upgrade would leave the device unbootable ("UBI init error 22"). That
rested on one unit that stopped booting after a scripted in-place
upgrade. It was never reproduced, and it does not hold.

On an RD03v2 with the stock loader, in-place sysupgrades with the
settings kept all booted: 3 times with the check removed (v2.1.2 to
v2.1.2, v2.1.1 and v2.1.2 again), once on the unmodified v2.1.2 with
sysupgrade -F overriding the check, and 3 more times with ubi_kernel
reformatted before nand_do_upgrade. In the 4 runs without the reformat,
nand_do_upgrade rewrote the kernel volume in place: ubi_kernel kept its
image sequence number while the kernel and layout volumes moved to
other eraseblocks.

The loader prints "UBI init error 22" whenever it tries slot 1.
With flag_last_success=0 and flag_try_sys1_failed=8 it starts rootfs_1
first, which on this layout is the first 36 MiB of OpenWrt's rootfs
UBI and cannot attach there, then falls back to slot 0. So on its own
the message does not show that the kernel UBI was the problem.

OpenWrt upgrades the AX6000 and the Redmi AX5400 in place, with this
NAND layout and this upgrade case, and has no such check for them.
Drop it. A
first install from stock still runs from the initramfs, where
xiaomi_initramfs_prepare reformats both UBI partitions.

Link: https://forum.openwrt.org/t/252985/29
---
 .../ipq50xx/base-files/lib/upgrade/platform.sh       | 12 +-----------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/base-files/lib/upgrade/platform.sh b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/base-files/lib/upgrade/platform.sh
index 9a78cfaff1..f8cb947deb 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/base-files/lib/upgrade/platform.sh
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/base-files/lib/upgrade/platform.sh
@@ -354,18 +354,8 @@ linksys_mx_pre_upgrade() {
 
 platform_check_image() {
 	case "$(board_name)" in
-	cudy,p5)
-		nand_do_platform_check "$(board_name)" "$1"
-		;;
+	cudy,p5|\
 	xiaomi,mi-router-ax3000t-v2)
-		# The stock U-Boot can only attach a kernel UBI that was freshly
-		# ubiformatted, which xiaomi_initramfs_prepare only does when
-		# running from the initramfs. An in-place sysupgrade leaves the
-		# device unbootable ("UBI init error 22").
-		if [ "$(rootfs_type)" != "tmpfs" ]; then
-			v "Boot the initramfs image and run sysupgrade from there."
-			return 1
-		fi
 		nand_do_platform_check "$(board_name)" "$1"
 		;;
 	*)
-- 
2.47.3

